obs The send met a peer's push and rebased. Their commit had folded %670 and %671 five minutes before mine, so my shelf is discarded and theirs adopted, and their row took the number the spine had offered me -- mine derives one above it, cited here by its stamp until the spine binds it. This is the evening's fourth overtake and the first of its kind: a duplicate FOLD rather than a duplicate repair. Tidying a pin collides exactly as work does, and nothing in the ledger shows a pin is being tidied any more than it shows a red is being worked.
scope one red booked and closed in my own lane, one surfaced as a gate, no peer tree touched
obs The hot pass over the staged tree closed guards_green=212 guards_red=3 guards_gated=2 with tree_moved=no. All three reds are pre-existing and none is mine to close: sow_allow_reach as above; stash_record over the nine standing stashes, which is REDS %636 and waits on Keaton's word; and standing_equipment itself, which reds because it mirrors the other two by name -- red_self rather than a third fault.
obs The cold pass closed guards_green=210 guards_red=5 guards_gated=2 with tree_moved=yes, and the movement was mine. Of the five, declared_ceiling and standing_equipment read a card that was momentarily over its bound mid-edit and both run GREEN by hand afterward; tracked_link read a half-written link set; stash_record reads the nine standing stashes; sow_allow_reach is the gate above. The hot pass over the staged tree is the reading that answers for what this commit ships.
